      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AMERICAN BLAZE NZ (2) finished third last start, beaten a head, in a nice return to form at this track over 1684m. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Leading hope in a similar race. SOUTH SIDE STORY NZ (10) had to dig deep to salute last time out over 2130m at Gloucester Park, getting home by just 2 metres. Hard to know where he gets from this slightly awkward draw. Beautifully placed and is sure to prove tough to beat again. WHATARETHEODDS (5) owns a good fresh record and races well both here and at the distance. MAJOR FREEWAY (1) was in the money two starts ago then things went wrong last start when he broke. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. If he get things right he can be in the money.",
